## Decision 5 Oct 2026 (surface method)
Owner requires: smooth joints, per-node width/leg thickness, edge-loop-style control, some sculpting, editable curves, and EVENTUALLY a real vertex editor (very important). Face/muzzle may need true mesh.
Plan: three layers, all driven by the node tree.
1. NODE SURFACE (Stage 2): nodes blend with a smooth union (soft-min) so joints are smooth; k = smoothness. Prototype: pony_smooth_nodes.html (GPU raymarch, untested on iPad). Per-node radius/scale/width.
2. PROFILE NODES (Stage 3-4): limbs/neck/muzzle follow a curve through nodes with ring profiles (width, depth, taper, rotation) = edge-loop-like control without a mesh.
3. BAKE TO MESH (Stage 6): extract a real mesh (marching cubes) from the node surface, then vertex/edge/face tools, loop cut, soft sculpt brush, mirror. Vertex weights come from node influence so the baked mesh still animates. Store as optional `mesh` per part in blockout/2 (schema addition, not yet written).
Status: viewer prototypes only (pony_2d_vs_3d.html faceted, pony_smooth_nodes.html smooth). Published smooth demo: https://claude.ai/artifact/UVt4fpr9yVCiErwJ456ekC
Open question: does the smooth demo run fast enough on the owner's iPad (it lowers resolution while dragging)?


## Physics decision 5 Oct 2026
Owner wants live-testable ragdoll in the game: collide with surfaces and other avatars, grab and drop, an object travels mouth -> throat -> stomach -> intestine -> out the back, bag/fluid hierarchy working, same game as lighting and the fluid pipeline.
Plan: custom position-based (Verlet/PBD) solver on the node spheres (nodes = particles, parent links = distance constraints, min-distance limits stop limbs folding, sphere-sphere + ground collision, finger-spring grab). No engine dependency, fits the node data.
Tract = a path through live body nodes (mouth, pharynx, esophagus, cardia, stomach, intestine, exit); a swallowed item follows it with a stomach dwell. Bag hierarchy (stomach/bladder/uterus under one peritoneal capacity) drives node scale so the smooth surface bulges. Not built yet: bag pressure/fluids, avatar-vs-avatar, lighting, the game's fluid pipeline (game code not seen this session).
Prototype: pony_ragdoll_lab.html (canvas, untested on iPad; the cube is a ball collider). Published: https://claude.ai/artifact/2MM7tthsWp163uPdkeCyfC
Content rule: reproductive anatomy and breeding mechanics apply to adult characters only.


## Cavity/fluid decision 5 Oct 2026
Stable-Tec_PassThrough_Proof.html (in this bundle, origin unclear, owner uploaded it) is the model for Stage 5. A body ellipsoid with an internal bag + tube is ONE signed-distance field; the picture and the liquid particles both use it, so openings are real. Sliders: hole open, squeeze tube, body deform, gravity tilt; side slice; counters (organ/tube/outside).
Use it to replace the polyline stand-in in pony_ragdoll_lab.html: throat, stomach, intestine, exit become hollow channels cut (smooth-subtracted) from the pony node surface. Bag hierarchy = capacity per bag under one peritoneal limit, driving node scale. Limits of the proof: one bag, one opening (no exit), no volume bookkeeping, O(n^2) particle collisions.

## Findings to remember
- Legacy data: stray "}" (fixed), neck gap 0.10 (fixed), rear y -0.03 (kept), no ears/tail/mane.
- Legacy math: positions use 2:1 projection (unit sphere -> 45.25 x 39.19 px) but radii drawn at 32 px => balls ~29% small. One camera must drive both.
- Viewer axis mapping: three = (x, z, y). Mirrored vs right-handed on purpose (matches legacy). Keep.

